Revision history for RabbitMQ::Connection

0.9
    - Publisher confirms: confirm_select(channel => N); send on a confirm-mode
      channel waits for settlement and returns "ack" | "returned" | "nack" |
      "timeout" (was: void). Non-confirm send returns "sent".
    - mandatory publications are settled correctly: basic.return followed by
      basic.ack reports "returned", never "ack"; last_return exposes the
      return's reply code/text, exchange, routing key and body length.
    - Confirm sequence numbers are tracked per channel.
    - Confirm mode is restricted to publish-only connections, enforced both
      ways: confirm_select refuses after consume, consume refuses after
      confirm_select.
    - connection.blocked / connection.unblocked are handled during settlement
      waits (is_blocked); channel.close / connection.close from the broker
      are answered with close-ok and croak.
    - Test suite against a live broker (t/, TEST_HOST) plus a docker harness
      (xt/docker-test.sh) covering every settlement outcome.

0.8
    - Configurable heartbeat.
